@host = http://localhost:5100

### Is this backend up?
GET {{host}}/health

### REQUIREMENT 11 - can this backend reach the Java one?
GET {{host}}/api/proxy/health

### Master data (public)
GET {{host}}/api/states

###
GET {{host}}/api/cities/state/1

###
GET {{host}}/api/hubs/all

### Customer registration
POST {{host}}/api/customer/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Customer",
  "email": "test.customer@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "password": "Password@123"
}

### Customer login - copy accessToken into @token below
POST {{host}}/api/customer/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test.customer@example.com", "password": "Password@123" }

### Staff login (any seeded staff account)
POST {{host}}/api/staff/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "yogesh.verma.visakhapatnam1@fleman.in", "password": "Password@123" }

@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Profile
GET {{host}}/api/customer/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Staff bookings - hub-scoped by default
GET {{host}}/api/staff/bookings?page=0&size=10&status=PENDING&scope=PICKUP
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Any booking by id - deliberately NOT hub-scoped
GET {{host}}/api/staff/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Forward an arbitrary GET to the Java service
GET {{host}}/api/proxy/forward?path=/api/states
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
